Computers have developed significantly overs the years. The use of computer is rapidly growing. The development of computer can be explained in three stages: past, present and future.
1.Computers in past
In the past computers were very large(room size), expensive, accuracy and operating speed was slow and had limited storage capacity. Computer uses the memory like paper tape, magnetic tape, magnetic drum. Thousands of vaccumm tubes used to be used as technology. Slowly it started to use transistor and integrated circuit. Past computers consumed high heat and power .Programming was difficult because often done by using machine language. Some examples of past computers are EDVAC, UNIVAC and EDSAC. They are mainly used by large organizations, university and governments.
2.Computers in present
Computers are now small in size (protable), easy to use, less expensive (affordable than previous computers) and has high processing and operating speed and has more storage capacity. Present modern computers used microprocessor/(VLSI) Very large scale integration as technology. Today's computers use memories like RAM, ROM, Cache memory. The electricity, power and comsumption is comparatively less than past computers. Programming is much easier because modern computers use high level programming language. They also supports AI, cloud and internet services, cybersecurity and automation. Laptops, desktops, and smartphones are commonly used. Computers are now used in every fileds like education, banking, business , healthcare etc.
3.Computers in Future
Future computers are expected to become more faster, smaller, intelligent and more connected. The operating speed will be in (LIPS) Logical inference per second and more than femto seconds. VVLSI or Bio-chips will be used as technology. The computer will be AI and AI will make computers more capable of learning and decision making. Computers may become more integrated with robots and smart devices. They will have advanced and distributed storage. Future computers will support more natural interaction i.e, the voice, gesture, and natural language interfaces may reduce the need for keyboards. Computers will increasingly support automation in all sectos like education, banking, transportation, healthcare, manufacturing etc. Thus, they will be more advance AI and autonomous systems.

